export default {"html":"<p data-line=\"0\" class=\"code-line\">These sites use Angular prerender and are hosted as static sites:</p>\n<p data-line=\"2\" class=\"code-line\"><a href=\"https://benaton.net/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://benaton.net/</a><a href=\"https://benaton.net/\" style=\"display:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://benaton.net/</a></p>\n<p data-line=\"4\" class=\"code-line\"><a href=\"https://concent-market.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://concent-market.com/</a><a href=\"https://concent-market.com/\" style=\"display:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://concent-market.com/</a></p>\n<p data-line=\"6\" class=\"code-line\">The owner updates content on GitHub. With raw HTML, it is easy to accidentally delete a <code>&gt;</code>; I have them edit TypeScript files instead so type checking fails when something breaks. Updates look like this:</p>\n<p data-line=\"8\" class=\"code-line\"><a href=\"https://github.com/le-benaton/website/blob/main/src/data/news.ts#L1-L12\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/le-benaton/website/blob/main/src/data/news.ts#L1-L12</a><a href=\"https://github.com/le-benaton/website/blob/main/src/data/news.ts#L1-L12\" style=\"display:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://github.com/le-benaton/website/blob/main/src/data/news.ts#L1-L12</a></p>\n<p data-line=\"10\" class=\"code-line\">Most other static sites I maintain are Angular as well. With few non-Angular dependencies, I ran <code>ng update</code> to Angular 19 right away. Here are two places I got stuck.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1.-%E2%9C%98-%5Berror%5D-ts2315%3A-type-'http2serverresponse'-is-not-generic.-%5Bplugin-angular-compiler%5D\" data-line=\"12\" class=\"code-line\"><a class=\"header-anchor-link\" href=\"#1.-%E2%9C%98-%5Berror%5D-ts2315%3A-type-'http2serverresponse'-is-not-generic.-%5Bplugin-angular-compiler%5D\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></a> 1. ✘ [ERROR] TS2315: Type 'Http2ServerResponse' is not generic. [plugin angular-compiler]</h2>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"14\"><span class=\"line\"><span>✘ [ERROR] TS2315: Type 'Http2ServerResponse' is not generic. [plugin angular-compiler]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    node_modules/@angular/ssr/node/index.d.ts:190:100:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>      190 │ ...rResponse | Http2ServerResponse&lt;Http2ServerRequest&gt;): Promise&lt;...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span></code></pre></div><p data-line=\"21\" class=\"code-line\">A type error. It looked like stale dependencies; reinstalling <code>node_modules</code> fixed it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"23\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">%</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> rm</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> -r</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> -f</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> node_modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> package-lock.json</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> &amp;&amp; </span><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">npm</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> i</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"2.-sass-%40import-rules-are-deprecated-and-will-be-removed-in-dart-sass-3.0.0.\" data-line=\"27\" class=\"code-line\"><a class=\"header-anchor-link\" href=\"#2.-sass-%40import-rules-are-deprecated-and-will-be-removed-in-dart-sass-3.0.0.\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></a> 2. Sass @import rules are deprecated and will be removed in Dart Sass 3.0.0.</h2>\n<p data-line=\"29\" class=\"code-line\">This is not a hard error, but Dart Sass now warns that current <code>@import</code> behavior will be removed in 3.0.0. Details are here:</p>\n<p data-line=\"31\" class=\"code-line\"><a href=\"https://sass-lang.com/documentation/breaking-changes/import/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://sass-lang.com/documentation/breaking-changes/import/</a><a href=\"https://sass-lang.com/documentation/breaking-changes/import/\" style=\"display:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://sass-lang.com/documentation/breaking-changes/import/</a></p>\n<p data-line=\"33\" class=\"code-line\">The <code>sass-migrator</code> package migrates files that trigger the warning:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"35\"><span class=\"line\"><span>$ npm install -g sass-migrator</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>$ sass-migrator module --migrate-deps your-entrypoint.scss</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span></code></pre></div><p data-line=\"40\" class=\"code-line\">If you only used <code>@import</code> like plain CSS, this migration is usually enough. If you relied heavily on mixins and Sass variables, it may be worth planning a move toward CSS variables and related rewrites.</p>\n<p data-line=\"42\" class=\"code-line\">See you next time.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"1.-%E2%9C%98-%5Berror%5D-ts2315%3A-type-'http2serverresponse'-is-not-generic.-%5Bplugin-angular-compiler%5D","text":"1. ✘ [ERROR] TS2315: Type 'Http2ServerResponse' is not generic. [plugin angular-compiler]","level":2},{"id":"2.-sass-%40import-rules-are-deprecated-and-will-be-removed-in-dart-sass-3.0.0.","text":"2. Sass @import rules are deprecated and will be removed in Dart Sass 3.0.0.","level":2}]} as const;
